---
description: KitGap project context and rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing code, read `docs/handoff.md` (project context, commands and the rules that must keep holding) and, for this Next.js version, the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.

- Every data change goes through `mutate()` in `src/server/services/core.ts`; check permissions in the service.
- Keep the quantity rules in `docs/quantity-model.md`; add tests for any change to quantities, permissions or privacy.
- Schema changes are new files in `db/migrations/`; never edit an applied migration.
- Never invent users, partners, statistics or impact claims.
- Run `npm run check` before calling a change done.
